{
  "text": " The 7th 1972 was the United States Marine Corps Chief Warrant Officer 3. He is one of two Marines to be captured as a prisoner of war, POW, twice. The first during World War II and the second during the Korean War, spending more than six years total in captivity. McHool held the record as the longest held Marine POW until surpassed by several other Marines during the Vietnam War. Early Life and World War II Felix J. McHool was born on June 14, 1912 in Pahau. The United States Marine Corps Chief Warrant Officer 3. He was captured as the longest held Marine POW until surpassed by several other Marines during the Vietnam War. The first during World War II Felix J. McHool was born on June 14, 1912 in Pahau. He was captured as the longest held Marine POW until surpassed by several other Marines during the Vietnam War.",
